30,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The staffing situation is precarious. Late-turn pools are thin and roadway crews are under-established, though lift maintenance has spare capacity.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Mid-city runs are slower than they used to be, but the real time-sink is waiting for connections, not the actual travel or ticketing.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Fascinating. We have a ring-fenced construction balance, but our operating and tech budgets are shrinking. Also, ticketing fees are eating our paving budget.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Servas,,"History shows that station rebuilds were successful, while lane-priority failed. Interestingly, a late-evening pilot from years ago was actually cost-effective.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I've found that work in old station shells is risky due to unrecorded voids, and there is a lack of agreement on data terms between ferry and rail.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if the late-evening pilot worked, we must consider if we have the staff now. My findings suggest we are relying heavily on overtime.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, if the tech budget is trimmed, maybe we shouldn't push for a complex new fare system if the audits show ticketing isn't the main delay.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, a fair point. If the money is ring-fenced for construction, a physical project might be more financially viable than a tech overhaul.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, the vitality of the network depends on its hours. If the pilot was a success, the demand is there, provided we solve the staffing.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, if construction is the way, we should be wary of the pre-war shells. The ""ground"" is hiding voids that cause weeks of delays.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, that makes station upgrades risky. However, the lift maintenance contract has spare capacity, which is a rare positive.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"If mid-city runs are slower but crowds clear, maybe a dedicated corridor is better than just adding more buses to the same traffic.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, but @Jonathan mentioned paving rates are climbing. A bus corridor with rebuilt islands might be prohibitively expensive right now.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Servas,,We must not repeat the mistake of the lane-priority stretches that were returned to mixed traffic. We need a plan that lasts.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,The joint operators' committee minutes suggest that any integrated fare system would face a bureaucratic wall between ferry and rail.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Asuka,,It seems the most stable option is one that utilizes existing maintenance capacity and avoids the most depleted crew pools.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Takumi,,I still think we need to address the connection times and the mid-city slowdown.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Logic suggests we avoid the tech line and the operating subsidy cuts. The ring-fenced construction fund is our strongest lever.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Servas,,Let us look for the path that balances historical success with current reality.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. We should avoid the pre-war shells and the data-sharing disputes.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
