55,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Candidate A is too risky for our current rosters. Candidate C aligns with our spare lift maintenance capacity.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Candidate B addresses the mid-city slowdown I found, though I worry about the paving costs Benjamin mentioned.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate D is out due to budget cuts in tech and the contractor fee issue. Candidate C uses the construction balance.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Candidate A has historical precedent for success, but Candidate C's type of work was also successful in the previous programme.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Candidate D is a nightmare of uncoordinated data. Candidate C is risky due to the shells, but B seems the most straightforward.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, B requires roadway crews, who are a third below establishment. C uses the lift crews who actually have capacity.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, that's a good point. If we can't staff the corridor, it won't work. Is C's impact on passenger time significant?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"C improves flow. Given the ring-fenced construction funds and the staffing alignment, C is the most rational choice.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Servas,,I agree. The accessibility records show these rebuilds finish within their windows. It is a proven path.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"If the lift maintenance is the only area with spare capacity, then C is the only plan that won't stall due to labor.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I am satisfied with C. It is the only one that doesn't exacerbate the staffing crisis.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"I'll concede. If B is unstaffable and D is unfunded, C is the best we can do for the passengers.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we have reached a logical consensus. C avoids the budget traps and the staffing voids.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Servas,,A wise choice. It builds on what we know works without overextending our tired crews.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I can support C, provided we are careful with the shell contingencies.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
